  "query_preview": "..\nThe trade-wind regime will continue for the Marianas. A brief trade-\nwind trough with minimal upper-level support will bring scattered \nshowers and potential isolated thunderstorms beginning after \nmidnight at Guam and Rota, then on Friday at Tinian and Saipan. \nShowers look to clear out Friday night, resuming the drier trade-wind\npattern throughout the remainder of the forecast period. Although \nrainfall is expected, it will not nearly be enough to offset the past\nfew weeks of little to no rainfall. Therefore, early water \nconservation efforts are encouraged as the dry season approaches, \nwhich could potentially introduce abnormally dry (D0) conditions to \nthe region within the next few weeks.",
